  <section id="mapping" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Type mapping</h2>
    <p>
      Spec 02 §1 maps Prisma types onto <code>drizzle-orm/sqlite-core</code>. Each table exports
      <code>xTable</code>, <code>type X</code> (select), and <code>type NewX</code> (insert).
      Relation objects are not generated up front. Add <code>relations()</code> on a table only
      when a query needs the relational API.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Prisma</th><th>Drizzle</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>String</code></td><td><code>text</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Int</code></td><td><code>integer</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Float</code></td><td><code>real</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Boolean</code></td><td><code>integer(&#123; mode: "boolean" &#125;)</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>DateTime</code></td><td><code>integer(&#123; mode: "timestamp_ms" &#125;)</code> (JS <code>Date</code> in and out)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Json</code></td><td><code>text(&#123; mode: "json" &#125;)</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Bytes</code></td><td><code>blob(&#123; mode: "buffer" &#125;)</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>enum</td><td><code>text(&#123; enum &#125;)</code> plus an exported <code>XValues</code> const and <code>X</code> union</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@default(cuid())</code></td><td><code>$defaultFn(newId)</code> using <code>crypto.randomUUID()</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@updatedAt</code></td><td><code>$defaultFn</code> and <code>$onUpdateFn</code> set to <code>new Date()</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>onDelete</code></td><td><code>.references(() =&gt; table.col, &#123; onDelete &#125;)</code>. Missing <code>onDelete</code> means restrict.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      JSON columns are <code>unknown</code> until a repository decodes them with a Schema from
      <code>@cadcamfun/api</code>. Spec 02 lists that as an open follow-up, along with indexes on
      hot foreign keys (<code>Project.ownerId</code>, <code>Toolpath.projectId</code>,
      <code>Drawing.projectId</code>).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="querying" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Querying</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Database.layer(&#123; path, migrationsFolder? &#125;)</code> is the only way to obtain a
      connection. It opens <code>bun:sqlite</code>, sets <code>PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL</code> and
      <code>PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON</code>, creates the parent directory, runs migrations when a
      folder is given, and closes the handle when the layer scope ends. Optional
      <code>backupsDirectory</code> defaults to <code>backups</code> beside the database.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="The contract other packages use">
{`import { Database, schema } from "@cadcamfun/db"

const { query } = yield* Database
const projects = yield* query("projects.list", (db) =>
  db.select().from(schema.projectTable)
)`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      The sidecar builds the layer once. The database file is
      <code>&lt;appData&gt;/cadcamfun/cadcamfun.db</code> (spec 02) from
      <code>CADCAMFUN_DATA_DIR</code>, at <code>&lt;dir&gt;/cadcamfun.db</code> (spec 05).
      Migrations run before the HTTP server listens. The migrations folder ships beside the
      compiled sidecar; WP5 and WP10 map <code>packages/db/drizzle/</code> to runtime
      <code>migrations/</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The CLI <code>bun run db:migrate</code> reads a path from <code>DATABASE_URL</code> and
      otherwise uses <code>./data/cadcamfun.db</code>. Spec 02 §3 says the untracked
      <code>.env*</code> files at the repo root are legacy and must not be used by v6. Do not
      read them. The local path for the app comes from sidecar config.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="upgrades" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Upgrades</h2>
    <p>
      Upgrade safety belongs to WP0. Before pending migrations on an existing file, SQLite
      <code>VACUUM INTO</code> writes a standalone WAL-consistent snapshot. New files and
      <code>:memory:</code> skip that backup. Names include a UTC timestamp. Only the last five
      snapshots for that database are kept. A backup or retention failure aborts startup as
      <code>DatabaseError</code> with operation <code>backup</code>. Migration failures use
      operation <code>migrate</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Pending SQL and journal updates run in one SQLite transaction. Failure preserves the
      original logical schema, data, and journal. Migration SQL must not contain transaction
      control or non-transactional statements such as <code>VACUUM</code>. Connection acquisition
      is scoped before initialization, so a failed start releases the handle. Shutdown attempts
      <code>wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE)</code> and always closes SQLite. Other packages must not
      close the handle. Concurrent upgrades from two sidecars are unsupported.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="tables" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Tables</h2>
    <p>
      <code>schema.ts</code> exports one <code>*Table</code> constant per SQLite table. Group them
      by what a caller is looking for. Better Auth tables (<code>Session</code>,
      <code>Account</code>, <code>Passkey</code>, <code>TwoFactor</code>,
      <code>Authenticator</code>, <code>VerificationToken</code>) are retained for a later cloud
      phase and unused by the v6.0 local profile.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Group</th><th>Tables</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Identity</td><td><code>User</code>, <code>Account</code>, <code>Session</code>, <code>Authenticator</code>, <code>VerificationToken</code>, <code>Passkey</code>, <code>TwoFactor</code>, <code>Subscription</code>, <code>ApiKey</code>, <code>Token</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Org and chat</td><td><code>Organization</code>, <code>OrganizationInvitation</code>, <code>UserOrganization</code>, <code>Conversation</code>, <code>ConversationParticipant</code>, <code>Message</code>, <code>Notification</code>, <code>PushSubscription</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Project model</td><td><code>Project</code>, <code>Drawing</code>, <code>DrawingVersion</code>, <code>Component</code>, <code>ComponentVersion</code>, <code>ComponentComment</code>, <code>Toolpath</code>, <code>ToolpathVersion</code>, <code>ToolpathComment</code>, <code>Material</code>, <code>Tool</code>, <code>MachineConfig</code>, <code>LibraryItem</code>, <code>FileUpload</code>, <code>ActivityLog</code>, <code>AIAnalysisLog</code>, <code>MeshAsset</code>, <code>CadOperationLog</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Costs and plugins</td><td><code>CostSettings</code>, <code>ProductionCostEstimate</code>, <code>ToolWearCost</code>, <code>MaterialCost</code>, <code>OperationCost</code>, <code>PluginRegistryEntry</code>, <code>PluginConfiguration</code>, <code>MCPServerConfig</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Marketplace</td><td><code>MarketplaceItem</code>, <code>MarketplaceSeller</code>, <code>MarketplaceOrder</code>, <code>MarketplaceReview</code>, <code>MarketplaceCategory</code>, <code>MarketplaceCollection</code>, <code>MarketplaceCollectionItem</code>, <code>MarketplaceWishlist</code>, <code>MarketplacePayout</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>History</td><td><code>GitRepo</code>, <code>GitObject</code>, <code>GitRef</code>, <code>PullRequest</code>, <code>PullRequestReview</code>, <code>WorkflowRun</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Native KV</td><td><code>LocalKeyValue</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      On first launch the sidecar <code>LocalProfile</code> service creates the single local
      <code>User</code> row (spec 02 gap, owned by WP4). Native CAM saves reuse
      <code>Toolpath</code> and <code>ToolpathVersion</code> JSON columns. Spec 02’s change log
      says that path needs no extra columns.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="boundaries" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Boundaries</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No package other than <code>packages/db</code> may import <code>bun:sqlite</code> or construct a Drizzle client.</li>
      <li>Callers must not close the SQLite handle. They retain the layer scope through shutdown.</li>
      <li>Generated SQL under <code>packages/db/drizzle/</code> must not be hand-edited.</li>
      <li>Credentials, GitHub tokens, and the per-launch bearer token must not be written into <code>LocalKeyValue</code> or any other table.</li>
      <li>v6 must not follow <code>DATABASE_URL</code> values from the legacy <code>.env*</code> files.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
